      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1741425
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-03T05:31:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a good question. There are different options.\n\n1. Put this pid in binder_context.\nPros: Each binder device can have its own listener.\nCons: That breaks KMI so it\u0027s not easy to port to different versions of ACK.\n\n2. Use a global one.\nPros: It doesn\u0027t touch any existing binder structures so it\u0027s easy to backport to other older kernels.\nCons: A unified process would listen to all binder instances (that\u0027s why the struct binder_report has a \"minor\" member)",
      "parentUuid": "31d29d98_4a33bc37",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 31
      },
